xnu 0224: the CP proves it consumed the bring-up before the ring is published

The same kernel brings the CP up two ways. Measured: in the boot that works
CP_RB_RPTR reaches 12 after the secure-mode switch and the 2000-submission
stress runs; in the boot that does not it stays at 11, the SQE halts on the
switch's own header (`cp sqe stat 0x649 0x70e60001`, ucode pc 0x224, its halt
loop) and no stress line appears at all. The ring was published anyway --
`mondrian_uc_up = 1` sat after the step's `if (rptr >= at)`, not inside it --
so MondrianGPU appeared, every later submission waited out its 300 ms, Mesa's
fd_pipe_new2 failed and the UI silently ran on softpipe: 26 fps, every frame
copied out. A boot with a dead CP has to say so instead.

The read pointer of every step is now read through one bounded helper
(`mondrian_cp_wait_rptr`, 2000 x 1 ms, the window the steps already had inline),
and the ring is published only once the CP has consumed the last bring-up
packet. A failure after the switch is retried once: the SQE is gated, a CP_NOP
goes into the dword it stopped on, the switch is re-issued behind it, and the
SQE is started again through the same raw CP_SQE_CNTL store the start uses,
after the same delay(20). It reuses the read pointer the SQE kept, writes no
GPU, GMU, GDSC or SMMU register, and is not a GPU reset: the CP register port
has just answered the CP_RB_RPTR reads that failed the check. `cpnoretry=1`
reports instead of retrying. If it still fails the ring stays unpublished and
`mondrian_gpu_uc_ready()` stays 0, so Mesa fails at pipe creation instead of
300 ms into the first frame.

What the next boot's log says:

	MONDRIAN GPU: cp secmode rptr 12 wptr 12
	MONDRIAN GPU: cp ready rptr 25 of 25
	    the CP consumed every bring-up packet; the healthy boot is unchanged
	    apart from the new `cp ready` line.
	MONDRIAN GPU: cp secmode rptr 11 wptr 12
	MONDRIAN GPU: cp secmode retry rptr 15 of 15
	    the race happened and the retry recovered it; the ring is published
	    and submissions fence.
	MONDRIAN GPU: cp NOT ready rptr 11 of 12, sqe 0x649 0x70e60001, ring not published
	    the CP is dead: MondrianGPU does not appear, so Mesa's open fails
	    immediately rather than every frame waiting out a fence.
